Engineering Rationale

Engineering Need

Adaptive vehicle intelligence requires a capability that can transform interpreted operating context into an appropriate response decision. Without a distinct decision-generation capability, responsibility for selecting responses would become coupled with contextual interpretation or physical execution.

---

Engineering Context

SO-F-004 occupies the decision-generation stage between operating-context interpretation and downstream action execution.

SO-F-003 establishes the interpreted operating context. SO-F-004 evaluates that context and relevant alternatives to generate an adaptive decision. The resulting decision is subsequently subject to applicable authorization and execution mechanisms.

---

Engineering Justification

Separating decision generation from interpretation allows contextual understanding to evolve independently from decision strategies.

Separating decision generation from execution prevents the mechanism responsible for determining what should happen from becoming responsible for physically carrying it out.

This separation supports modular architecture, clearer verification boundaries, independent evolution of decision strategies, and improved traceability from decisions to the contextual conditions that informed them.

---

Generated Decision and Authorization

A decision generated by SO-F-004 shall not automatically be considered authorized for execution.

The distinction allows authority, safety, governance, and other applicable constraints to be represented through appropriate architectural mechanisms without embedding those mechanisms prematurely within the decision-generation objective.

The final authority architecture shall be established through subsequent architectural investigation and approved engineering decisions.

---

Expected Engineering Benefit

Achievement of this objective enables the system to:

- Generate adaptive responses from interpreted operating context.
- Evaluate alternative responses against applicable constraints.
- Maintain separation between understanding, decision generation, authorization, and execution.
- Support traceable decision-making.
- Permit future evolution of decision strategies without unnecessarily modifying perception or interpretation capabilities.

---

Dependencies and Assumptions

This objective depends on the interpreted operating context established by SO-F-003.

It may also depend on constraints, priorities, authority information, and other governing inputs established by separate approved architectural elements.

Execution of an approved decision remains outside the responsibility of SO-F-004 and belongs to the downstream execution capability.
